-- title:
--   Hecke stability of two-cusp ℤ₍ₚ₎-integrality, weight two
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a natural number $M \neq 0$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ be a subgroup containing every unit whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is trivial. Write $\Gamma_H(M)$ for the subgroup [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) of $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$, namely the image in $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ of the preimage of $H$ under the character $\Gamma_0(M) \to (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ given by the lower right entry mod $M$, and let $A \subseteq \mathbb{C}$ be the image under $\mathbb{Q} \to \mathbb{C}$ of the subring $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)} = \{x \in \mathbb{Q} : \gcd(\mathrm{den}(x),p) = 1\}$. Let $f$ be a cusp form of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_H(M)$ and assume that for every Atkin–Lehner datum $W$ for $(M,p)$ — a factorisation $M = pR$ together with integers $a,b$ satisfying $pa - Rb = 1$ — and every $n \in \mathbb{N}$, the $n$-th coefficient of the width-one $q$-expansion of $f$ and the $n$-th such coefficient of $f \mid_2 W$ (slash by the real matrix attached to $W$) both lie in $A$. The conclusion is that $f$ belongs to [`CuspForm.twoCuspIntegralSet M H 2 p A`](def/CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice.html#L54): for every element $t$ of the subring of $\mathbb{C}$-endomorphisms of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_H(M)$ generated by the Hecke generators `heckeGenH`, every Atkin–Lehner datum $W$ for $(M,p)$ and every $n$, the $n$-th $q$-expansion coefficients of $t f$ and of $(t f)\mid_2 W$ lie in $A$.
--
--   This is the $p$-local form of the statement that two-cusp integrality of weight-two forms — integrality of the Fourier coefficients at the cusp $\infty$ and at the cusp reached by the Atkin–Lehner involution at $p$ — is stable under the whole Hecke algebra, so that the naive integrality condition already cuts out a Hecke-stable lattice. It is used when producing an element of the two-cusp lattice with prescribed $q$-expansion coefficients, in the construction of the integral structures on which the mod $p$ reduction of weight-two forms of level $\Gamma_H(M)$, $p \parallel M$, is read.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_mem_twoCuspIntegralSet_ratLocalizedAt_of_forall_qCoeff_mem.lean

